From cd02e446ac592e28a06dc6cf76431f316af9fd96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 05:16:16 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 138/143] project: a C string the host sets by name is a
 string, not true

wp_project_property_set_value_by_name, _text_by_name, _combo_by_name, _file_by_name and _scene_texture_by_name (and
their wp_project_property_* twins) pass their `const char*` to Project::propertySet, whose overloads take a
std::string, a float, a glm::vec4 or a bool. A pointer converts to bool by a standard conversion, which beats the
user-defined one to std::string, so every one of them called the bool overload: a text, a combo key or a texture the
host set became `true`, its string "". liascape's scene worker sets every string-valued property this way.

Project gains `const char*` overloads of both propertySet families that forward to the std::string ones.

Tested by liascape's host_api_test string_values_set_by_name (a textinput and a scenetexture read back what was
set; before: "" for both).

Origin: ours
Why: liascape docs/TODO.md #108 (preset wallpapers: a preset's own images; found setting one)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Vg3T4kUDe36Q9Hthaz2WEU
---
 src/core/WallpaperEngine/Project.h | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Project.h b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Project.h
index 1493ed5..d59377b 100644
--- a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Project.h
+++ b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Project.h
@@ -53,6 +53,12 @@ public:
     void propertySet (const std::string& key, float value);
     void propertySet (const std::string& key, glm::vec4 value);
     void propertySet (const std::string& key, bool value);
+    // a C string is a string: without these, a `const char*` converts to bool before std::string and takes the bool
+    // overloads (every text, combo key and texture the host set became `true`)
+    void propertySet (const wp_project_property* property, const char* value) {
+	this->propertySet (property, std::string (value));
+    }
+    void propertySet (const std::string& key, const char* value) { this->propertySet (key, std::string (value)); }
 
     void describe (wp_describe_callback* callback);
 
